 "notes": "CR 103.5, the London mulligan. Each library holds exactly seven cards, so every draw of seven takes all of them whatever the shuffle. Seat 0 (the starting player) declares a mulligan, then seat 1 keeps. Seat 0's mulligan shuffles its hand into its library, draws seven again and puts one card on the bottom (A One). Seat 0 mulligans again: A One comes back with the redrawn seven, and two cards go to the bottom, each under the last (A Two, then A Three beneath it). Seat 0 keeps five; seat 1 kept its seven. The six Library cards are the runner's filler, added on top after the first turn begins."
